  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The number of $\\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}$ ions replacing $\\mathrm{x} \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}$ ions $=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{x}}{3}$ vacancies of cations\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n=x-\\frac{2 x}{3}=x / 3 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\text { But } x / 3=1-0.94=0.06, x=0.06 \\times 3 \\\\\r\n\r\n=0.18=18 \\%\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$",
